                <pb facs="0921" n="785" sameAs="frus:frus1929v01/pg785"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">723.2515/3360: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Peru</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Moore</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-05-01T16:00:00-04:00">May 1, 1929—4
                    p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>51. Your 87, April 30, 3 p.m., paragraph two. There must be a mistake regarding
                    this as Ambassador Davila has not called at the Department for over a week, that
                    is not since prior to the time this question came up.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
